{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["וישלח את אחיו — every root of לויה in doubled form is an expression of sending; the corresponding form in weak form is an expression of accompanying." "אל תרגזו — do not be afraid at all on the road because of bandits, for there is peace from every side. Similarly: ״רגזו ואל תחטאו״ — be afraid of the Holy One, blessed be He, and do not sin. Similarly: ״ונתן ה׳ לך לב רגז״ — דחיל in Targum. Similarly: ״ירגזון יריעות״ — an expression of trembling, like a person who is afraid. Similarly: ״רגזה בוטחות״ — who shakes the earth from its place. But the רגזה of the Targum of Daniel and of Ezra is an expression of anger. טרנב״ל is the Aramaic translation of רוגז of the twenty-four books."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {1 "The term לויה likely refers to the root לו\"ש (as in ויולך/לוות); 'doubled form' (משקל דגוש) vs. 'weak form' (משקל רפי) describes morphological patterns. The abbreviation טרנב״ל (טורנס/טרגומא) is rendered here as a term for the Aramaic translation tradition."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:23.512404357Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}